{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817844-dragonblood-3e-conversion-peach","id":817844,"title":"Dragonblood 3E conversion [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-27T12:43:45-08:00","id":817844,"title":"Dragonblood 3E conversion [PEACH]","content":"Aspects<br /> <br /> Air<br /> Aspect Abilities: Linguistics, Lore, Occult, Stealth, Thrown, Socialize, Craft<br /> Anima: An Aspect of Air can spend five motes to attune his anima to the winds. For the duration of a scene, the Exalt is surrounded by a swirling vortex of air, which functions as a weakened version of the Stormwind Rider spell. The Dragon-Blood may triple his leaping distance, and he takes no damage from falls, as gusts buoy him and slow his descent. Finally, the Dragon-Blooded may add his Essence to his Defense Value against Thrown and Archery attacks, as the winds buffet ranged weapons in order to protect their master.<br /> <br /> Earth<br /> Aspect Abilities: Awareness, Craft, Integrity, Resistance, War, Medicine, Survival<br /> Anima: An Aspect of Earth can spend five motes to attune his or her anima to the nearby stone, taking on the durability of the earth itself. For the duration of the scene, the Exalt gains Hardness equal to her Essence. She may also add her Essence to the difficulty of gambits to grapple or knock her back. Finally, she may add her Essence to her Stamina for all purposes, but only while her feet rest on either earth or stone.<br /> <br /> Fire<br /> Aspect Abilities: Athletics, Dodge, Melee, Presence, Socialize, War, ??Resistance??<br /> Anima: At the expenditure of five motes of Essence, the Children of Hesiesh can draw on their inner passions, forcing their anima banner to erupt. For the duration of the scene, the Exalt is surrounded by a corona of flames, which inflicts no damage on his body or possessions but affects anything else he touches as normal flames would. Any bare-handed or grappling attacks against the Exalt cause the attacker to suffer a number of initiative damage dice equal to the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence, and any similar attacks made by the Dragon-Blood inflict an additional number of damage dice equal to his Essence as well. The Exalt can also ignite flammable materials with a touch.<br /> <br /> Water<br /> Aspect Abilities: Bureaucracy, Investigation, Larceny, Martial Arts, Sail, Stealth, Socialize<br /> Anima: At the cost of five motes of Essence, the child of Daana\u2019d suffuses her being with the power of Water. For the duration of a single day, the Exalt has complete water freedom. She can breathe water as easily as air and is incapable of drowning. She also suffers no environmental penalty for any actions she takes underwater, including such improbable actions as firing a bow or throwing a chakram. As a final bonus, the Exalt can walk across the surface of a body of water as easily as dry land.<br /> <br /> Wood<br /> Aspect Abilities: Archery, Medicine, Performance, Ride, Survival, Craft, Stealth<br /> Anima: At a cost of five motes, the Wood Aspect can align his Essence with the power of all growing things. For the duration of a scene, the Exalt can render himself completely immune to the effects of any plant-based poison. This power is reflexive, and the Exalt need not know that he has been poisoned prior to activating this power. Indeed, while this effect is active, the Dragon-Blood becomes a walking plant toxin. If the Exalt makes skin-to-skin contact with someone, a difficulty 3 gambit while in combat, while this power is active, the target\u2019s player must make a successful (Stamina + Resistance) roll against a difficulty equal to the Exalt\u2019s Essence or suffer the effects of poisoning. Finally, the Dragon-Blood can add his Essence to his Defense Value against Archery attacks and any attacks using wooden or wood-hafted weapons, as the wooden shafts themselves struggle to avoid hitting the Exalt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:44:59-08:00","id":817846,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">DYNASTS OF THE BLESSED ISLE</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP ONE: CHARACTER CONCEPT</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose concept, elemental aspect and Motivation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Note aspect\u2019s anima powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP TWO: CHOOSING ATTRIBUTES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Note that all nine Attributes start with one dot automatically before you assign any.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prioritize your Attribute categories: Physical (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina); Social (Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance); and Mental (Perception, Intelligence, Wits). You have 7 dots to assign to your primary Attribute category, 6 to assign to your secondary, and 4 to place in the tertiary category.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP THREE: CHOOSING ABILITIES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose 5 Aspect Abilities.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Select Favored Abilities (3; may not be the same as Aspect Abilities.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose Abilities (35\u2014at least 13 must be from Aspect or Favored Abilities; at least one dot must be in each Favored Ability; none may be higher than 3 without spending bonus points. Dynastic characters must have at least Archery \u2022, Lore \u2022\u2022, Martial Arts \u2022, Melee \u2022, Performance \u2022, Presence \u2022, Ride \u2022, Socialize \u2022\u2022 and War \u2022.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP FOUR: ADVANTAGES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose Merits (15), Charms (10 Dragon-Blooded Charms, Immaculate martial artists get 7 Immaculate Martial Arts Charms instead, all of which must be from the same elemental tree, for which they get the Martial Arts merit(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) for free).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP FIVE: FINISHING TOUCHES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Record Essence rating (1), Personal Essence pool (Essence + 11), Peripheral Essence pool ([Essence x 4] + 23), Health Levels (-0, -1, -1, -2, -2, -4, Incapacitated), and Willpower (5).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 BONUS POINTS</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Spend bonus points (15) at any point during character creation.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:45:45-08:00","id":817847,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">LOOKSHY\u2019S TERRESTRIALS</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP ONE: CHARACTER CONCEPT</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose concept, elemental aspect and Motivation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Note Aspect\u2019s anima powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP TWO: CHOOSING ATTRIBUTES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Note that all nine Attributes start with one dot automatically before you assign any.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prioritize your Attribute categories: Physical (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina); Social (Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance); and Mental (Perception, Intelligence, Wits). You have 7 dots to assign to your primary Attribute category, 6 to assign to your secondary one, and 4 to place in the tertiary category.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP THREE: CHOOSING ABILITIES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose 5 Aspect Abilities.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Select Favored Abilities (3; may not be the same as Aspect Abilities).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Choose Abilities (35\u2014at least 13 must be from Aspect or Favored Abilities; at least one must be in each Favored Ability; none may start higher than 3 without spending bonus points)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Characters born in Lookshy must have a minimum of Archery \u2022\u2022, Linguistics \u2022\u2022\u2022, Lore \u2022\u2022, Martial Arts \u2022\u2022, Melee \u2022\u2022, Performance \u2022, Presence \u2022, Ride \u2022, Stealth \u2022 and War \u2022\u2022. Exiles or defectors from the Realm use Dynast character-creation rules except for Merits, which they purchase as if they were from Lookshy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP FOUR: SELECT ADVANTAGES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Chose Merits (13), Charms (Lookshy characters all start play with Wind-Carried Word Technique and Elemental Bolt Attack, to which they add 9 Dragon-Blooded Charms, Lookshy\u2019s Dragon-Blooded may not start play with Immaculate Martial Arts Charms, but may learn them later on, provided they can find someone to teach them)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 STEP FIVE: FINISHING TOUCHES</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Record Essence rating (1), Personal Essence pool (Essence + 11), Peripheral Essence pool ([Essence x 4] + 23), Health Levels (-0, -1, -1, -2, -2, -4, Incapacitated), and Willpower (5).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 BONUS POINTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Spend bonus points (15) at any point during character creation.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:46:34-08:00","id":817848,"title":"","content":"OUTCASTES<br /> <br /> \u2022 STEP ONE: CHARACTER CONCEPT<br /> Determine why your character has not joined the Realm or Lookshy.<br /> Choose aspect and Motivation.<br /> Note the anima powers provided by character\u2019s aspect.<br /> <br /> \u2022 STEP TWO: CHOOSING ATTRIBUTES<br /> Note that all nine Attributes start with one dot automatically before you assign any.<br /> Prioritize your Attribute categories: Physical (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina); Social (Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance); and Mental (Perception, Intelligence, Wits). You have 7 dots to assign to your primary Attribute category, 6 to assign to your secondary one, and 4 to place in the tertiary category.<br /> <br /> \u2022 STEP THREE: CHOOSING ABILITIES<br /> Choose 5 Aspect and 5 Favored Abilities: Outcastes start with 25 Ability points, at least 13 of which must be from Aspect or Favored Abilities; at least one dot must be in each Favored Ability; none may be higher than 3 without spending bonus points.<br /> <br /> \u2022 STEP FOUR: ADVANTAGES<br /> Choose Merits (7), Charms (10 Dragon-Blooded Charms, an outcaste who opts to learn Celestial martial arts get 7 Celestial Martial Arts Charms instead, all of which must be from the same elemental tree, thought unlike the Dynasts, they do not get the Martial Arts Merit for free)<br /> <br /> \u2022 STEP FIVE: FINISHING TOUCHES<br /> Record Essence rating (1), Personal Essence pool (Essence + 11), Peripheral Essence pool ([Essence x 4] + 23), Health Levels (-0, -1, -1, -2, -2, -4, Incapacitated), and Willpower (5).<br /> <br /> \u2022 BONUS POINTS<br /> Spend bonus points (15) at any point during character creation.<br /> <br /> TRAIT COST<br /> Primary or Secondary Attribute 4 per dot<br /> Tertiary Attribute 3 per dot<br /> Caste/Favored Ability 1 per dot<br /> Non-Caste/Favored Ability 2 per dot<br /> Specialty 1<br /> Merits 1 per dot<br /> Aspect/Favored Charm 6<br /> Non-Aspect/Favored Charm 8<br /> Immaculate/Celestial Martial Arts 11 (8 if favored/aspect)<br /> Evocation 4<br /> Willpower 2 per dot<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:47:50-08:00","id":817851,"title":"","content":"Merits<br /> <br /> Arsenal(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Lookshy &amp; Dynast Only<br /> Equipment borrowed from the Realm, your Family, your Legion. Although their use is granted to the character, they remain the property of that organization and must be returned\u2014in functioning order\u2014on demand. Dots provided by Arsenal may be used to purchase artifacts or hearthstones, with a maximum level per artifact equal to the rating in Arsenal. It also provides Resources that can be used for mundane equipment. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 194px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Artifact levels</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Resources</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">15</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">25</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">40</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">60</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">85</td> </tr> </table></div> Artifact(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Outcaste use the Merit as written in Exalted<br /> Lookshy &amp; Dynast Only<br /> The Artifact Background grants Terrestrials twice the number of dots worth of artifacts as normal, although any single artifact cannot exceed the Dragon-Blood\u2019s rating in Artifact. (A character with Artifact 3 cannot buy a four-dot artifact, but he can buy two three-dot artifacts.) Even Dragon-Blood with no rating in this Background will have a single one-dot artifact of the Storyteller\u2019s choice, so prevalent are jade wonders in these places.<br /> <br /> Breeding \u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Increased your Maximum mounts based on the table below. At the 4th level it costs 1 less mote to activate your anima banner and the 5th 2 less motes. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 192px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Personal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Peripheral</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Motes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Motes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">7</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">9</td> </tr> </table></div> Command(\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Lookshy and Dynasts Only<br /> <br /> Connections(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Lookshy and Dynasts Only<br /> Contacts + Influence<br /> <br /> Contacts (\u2022,\u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Outcaste Only<br /> <br /> Cult(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Realm characters only receive half benefit from this Merit.<br /> <br /> Family(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Lookshy and Dynasts Only<br /> Each dot in this Merit represents an immediate Dragon-Blooded relative or ancestor of some fame (or infamy). The player should work with their Storyteller to determine the nature, sex and status of the relation. It should be a blood relation no more than a generation or two removed, although exceedingly historic acts can resonate down four or more generations (and multiple centuries). The player should also determine what the character\u2019s notable relative was famous for (and in what context). The character receives a one-die bonus to all social dice pools where the relative\u2019s reputation could be relevant.<br /> <br /> Follower(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Outcaste Only<br /> <br /> <br /> Influence(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Outcaste Only<br /> <br /> Henchmen(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Dynasts Only<br /> A number of un-Exalted characters of note have sworn oaths of fealty to the character. The Exalt has 3 companions per level in this merit.<br /> <br /> Retainers(\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Lookshy and Dynasts Only<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:48:29-08:00","id":817853,"title":"","content":"OTHER RULES<br /> A number of other, minor rules govern the use of Dragon- Blooded characters. Where these rules do not specifically say otherwise, Dragon-Blooded are treated exactly as any other sort of Exalted. This includes but is not limited to the rate at which they heal, their resistance to poison and disease, their ability to suppress bleeding, the speed at which they regain Essence, the visibility and size of their anima banner and the rate at which it dissipates.<br /> <br /> ANIMA FLUX<br /> The anima banner of the Dragon-Blooded is a raw, powerful effect. While those of the other Exalted can be intense, and even have lasting impact on their environment, that of the Terrestrials can be so powerful as to inflict considerable damage on their surroundings. The effects of the damage is different for each type of Terrestrial, but the source is always the raw power of the character\u2019s Essence.<br /> <br /> If the Dragon-Blood\u2019s anima banner is Glowing, it inflicts one initiative damage for every turn to everyone within a number of feet equal to the character\u2019s permanent Essence, characters in initiative crash suffer 1 Lethal damage. This damage is sufficient to destroy cloth and soft wood in a minute or two. It can eventually reduce even treated hardwoods to junk.<br /> <br /> At the Burning level, the banner inflicts two points of damage every turn. At these two levels, being with Essence greater than or equal to the Terrestials do not suffer from these effects.<br /> <br /> At the Iconic level, however, the banner generates 3 damage to anyone affected by the first two levels and 1 to all others.<br /> <br /> SWORN BROTHERS\u2019 OATH<br /> Cost: Ritual, 2 WP<br /> Target: Exalts to be bound<br /> This Terrestrial Circle spell binds the Essences of a group of Exalts together and is used in the creation of sworn brotherhoods. The ritual takes one hour for a pair of Exalts, plus one hour for each additional Exalt. The sorcerer does not have to be one of the Exalted bound by the spell. The spell creates a Major intimacy of Loyalty to the brotherhood<br /> \u2022 Familiarity: Members of a sworn brotherhood are aware of each others\u2019 location. As long as a member of the brotherhood is within (Intimacy level x 10) yards of another member, she knows exactly where he is. Beyond this range, a member\u2019s player can make an Essence roll as a diceless action for the Exalt to get an idea of the direction and range to any other member. One success gives the sister a general idea of distance and direction, three is sufficient to get an accurate read on range and bearing, and five successes tell the sister exactly where her brother is.<br /> \u2022 Devotion: Each member of the sworn brotherhood gains a Devotion dice pool, equal to their intimacy rating, which refreshes once per story. These dice can be used\u2014in any amount as non-charm dice\u2014on actions undertaken with the deliberate purpose of aiding another member of the brotherhood.<br /> \u2022 Loyalty: If a members Intimacy of loyalty to the brotherhood is ever removed completely, she is removed from the brotherhood immediately<br /> <br /> A sorcerer is limited to binding no more Dragon Bloods into a single sworn brotherhood than an amount equal to twice his Essence, and an Exalt cannot be a member of more than one brotherhood.<br /> <br /> THE GREAT CURSE<br /> Dragon-blooded do not have Limit triggers and therefore Limit Break far less often.<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Excellencies:<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded can use their Essence to fortify their mortal skills much as the Solar Exalted can. While the heights of prowess they can attain are not as high, they can seize triumph from the jaws of defeat with great exertion of will. The maximum number of dice they can add to a roll is equal to the Ability used, +1 if they have an applicable specialty. After making a roll, the Dragon-Blood may pay a point of Willpower to reroll up to (Essence) dice that came up failures, paying one mote for each rerolled die. Thus, an Essence 2 Dragon-Blooded with Dexterity 5, Melee 5 (Specialty: Swords) could raise his melee dice pools by up to +6 dice. After rolling, he could spend one point of Willpower and up to two motes to re-roll two failed dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:50:52-08:00","id":817855,"title":"","content":"Linguistics<br /> <br /> LANGUAGE-LEARNING RITUAL<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Linguistics 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One Week<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> CIPHER MISSIVE<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Linguistics 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute, Written Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Language-Learning Ritual<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> CRAFT ICON<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute, Written Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cipher Missive<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> THOUSAND TONGUES MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Language-Learning Ritual<br /> Penalty not reduced by essence. Repurchase at 3 to halve penalty. Repurchase at 5 to remove penalty.<br /> <br /> POISONED TONGUE TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: 2m, 1wp, Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The Exalt may attempt an action that would be defended with resolve on someone in a conversation they are eavesdropping on without having to enter the conversation themselves or the target even being aware of them. The target receives a +2 bonus to their resolve against this action.<br /> Repurchase at 5 to remove bonus to targets resolve.<br /> <br /> VOICE OF MASTERY<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Linguistics 5, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Poisoned Tongue Technique<br /> Change Parry MDV to Resolve.<br /> <br /> WIND-CARRIED WORDS TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: 1m per message, plus distance; Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> VOICES ON THE WIND<br /> Cost: 3+ motes; Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One minute<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Wind-Carried Words Technique<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> SPEECH WITHOUT WORDS<br /> Cost: 2m + 1m per ally; Mins: Linguistics 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cipher Missive, Voices on the Wind<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> WITH ONE MIND<br /> Cost: 2 motes per dot of increase; Mins: Linguistics 5, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Combo-Basic<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Voice of Mastery, Voices on the Wind<br /> Replace last sentence of first paragraph with: May flurry a Defend Other action protecting one of the others enhanced by this charm without the normal -3 penalty for flurry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:53:03-08:00","id":817858,"title":"","content":"Lore<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL CONCENTRATION TRANCE<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Lore 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One day<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> ETERNAL MIND MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 2m, 1wp; Mins: Lore 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Elemental Concentration Trance<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL EMPOWERMENT MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 1+wp; Mins: Lore 5, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Elemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Elemental Concentration Trance<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL SUCCOR METHOD<br /> Cost: 5m and 1wp per lhl; 2 motes per hl; Mins: Lore 5, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Elemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Elemental Empowerment Meditation<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL BOLT ATTACK<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Lore 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Cooperative, Elemental, Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> This is an attack made with Athletics or Archery, Accuracy bonus equal to the Exalts Essence, with a range in range bands equal to the Exalts Essence, Overwhelming equal to half the Exalts Stamina, and a damage bonus equal to the Exalts Stamina + Essence.<br /> Air Aspects gain can fire one additional range band<br /> Fire Aspects gain +2 bonus damage<br /> Water Aspects force a -2 to soak or -1 to hardness<br /> Earth Aspects gain +1 to Overwhelming<br /> Wood Aspects gain +1 Accuracy<br /> <br /> Multiple Dragon-Bloods who know this Charm can combine their powers to generate a bolt of exceptional power. One Exalt (usually the one with the best attack pool or the one with the highest Stamina rating) must serve as the focus, with his (Dexterity + [Athletics or<br /> Archery]) used to determine the base attack pool. The Accuracy bonus of the attack is based on the Essence of the focus but gains a +1 bonus per additional participant. Finally, the elemental side effects of each separate aspect who aids in this Charm are inflicted upon the target. If multiple Dragon-Blooded of the same aspect aid in this Charm, however, their special elemental effect is applied only once.<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL BURST TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: 8m; Mins: Lore 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Cooperative, Elemental, Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Elemental Bolt Attack<br /> As above but hits everyone within a number of range bands equal to the users Essence. One attack roll is made and compared to all defenses. Same bonuses as above. Can be done cooperatively as above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:54:12-08:00","id":817861,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Occult</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">TERRESTRIAL CIRCLE SORCERY</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: -- Mins: Occult 4, Essence 2; </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">As the Solar version.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">SPIRIT-DETECTING MIRROR TECHNIQUE</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: 2m; Mins: Occult 3, Essence 1; </span></span></span><br /> <sp