r /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Remove &quot;If he uses a Combo, he must pay the surcharge on each individual Charm that makes up the Combo.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:00:34-08:00","id":817878,"title":"","content":"Craft<br /> <br /> SHAPING HAND STYLE<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Craft 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One hour<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Remove &quot;The Charm can be used to transform the Dragon-Blood\u2019s hand into a deadly weapon such as a hammer or a pickaxe, adding a maximum of +2 bashing or +1 lethal to her unarmed attacks, depending on whether the tool is bladed or not.&quot;<br /> <br /> STONE-CARVING FINGERS FORM<br /> Cost: -- Mins: Craft 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Shaping Hand Style<br /> The Exalt gains a free full excellency when working primarily with stone/rock.<br /> PERFECT CLIMBING ATTITUDE<br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Stone-Carving Fingers Form<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> FLAW-FINDING EXAMINATION<br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One minute<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> When performing a basic repair project the interval is reduced to one turn. A major repair projects interval is reduced to one minute.<br /> <br /> FLAW-FINDING EXPLOITATION<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive only<br /> Duration: One minute<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flaw-Finding Examination<br /> This charm supplements a disarm gambit. If successful it destroys the weapon.<br /> <br /> CHARM OF LESSER UNMAKING<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 2; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flaw-Finding Examination<br /> The Exalt gains craft experience equal to half what they would have gained for creating the item.<br /> <br /> CHARM OF GREATER UNMAKING<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 4; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Combo-Basic<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Charm of Lesser Unmaking<br /> The Exalt gains craft experience equal to half what they would have gained for creating the item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:02:24-08:00","id":817880,"title":"","content":"Integrity<br /> <br /> UNSLEEPING EARTH MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Integrity 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One day<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> UNTIRING EARTH MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Integrity 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One day<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Unsleeping Earth Meditation<br /> Change 6 ticks to one turn<br /> <br /> OATH OF THE TEN-THOUSAND DRAGONS<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Integrity 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The character swears an oath and gains a major intimacy of loyalty to a group. Weakening this intimacy requires the use of another major intimacy rather than a minor. This charm may be purchased multiple times for multiple groups.<br /> <br /> TEN-THOUSAND DRAGONS FIGHT AS ONE<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Integrity 3, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration:<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Oath of the Ten-Thousand Dragons<br /> This can be used to instantly form a minor positive intimacy to a fellow Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> UNFLAGGING VENGEANCE MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp (additional allies must each pay 1wp); Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Social<br /> Duration: Until satisfied<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Untiring Earth Meditation, Ten-Thousand Dragons Fight as One<br /> To activate this Charm, the Exalt must spend three motes and one Willpower while speaking aloud the terms of a vendetta to which the character commits himself with all his soul. The goal<br /> must be a simply stated purpose such as \u201cAvenge my father\u2019s death at the hands of Tepet Arada\u201d or \u201cHumble Sesus Chenow Lahor for his insult on my honor.\u201d Swearing such an oath provides the Dragon-Blood with several benefits.<br /> First, for as long as the vendetta lasts, it counts as an major Intimacy for the Dragon-Blood with all the benefits and drawbacks of any Intimacy. Second, whenever confronted by any effect, magical or otherwise, that might deter the Dragon-Blood from pursuing his vengeance, he adds his Essence to his Resolve . Furthermore, he can ignore any unnatural influence that would compel him to abandon the vendetta, treating such commands as unacceptable orders. Third, until the Exalt fulfills the vendetta or abandons it, he does not need to eat, sleep or rest as long as he remains in pursuit of his vengeance. The character incurs no penalties from any sort of fatigue, whether natural, magical or even from encumbrance or armor. Fourth, the Exalt Integrity to both his natural soak.<br /> Unflagging Vengeance Meditation can be sustained without ill effect for a number of days equal to the Exalt\u2019s Essence. After that, the character suffers one health bashing damage every time a number of days equal to his Essence passes. This damage cannot be healed while the Charm remains in force, and even after the Charm lapses, healing this damage takes twice as long as normal. When a Dragon-Blood swears a vendetta with this Charm, a number of additional characters equal to his Essence can join him. Each additional participant must pay one temporary Willpower point but need not expend any Essence. Once invoked, the Charm ends either when the vendetta is satisfied or when the Dragon-Blood who initiated it voluntarily abandons it. If anyone who is party to the Charm, including the Dragon-Blood who initiated it, terminates his involvement prematurely, he suffers a number of levels of lethal damage equal to the sum of the permanent Essences of all characters involved.<br /> <br /> GRANITE CURTAIN OF SERENITY<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Ten-Thousand Dragons Fight as One<br /> For the duration of a scene, The Dragon-Blood adds his Essence to his Resolve versus any supernatural effect against that seeks to sway his emotions, control his mind or induce madness.<br /> <br /> INVIOLATE DRAGON SPIRIT<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp, 1 hl; Mins: Integrity 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Ten-Thousand Dragons Fight as One<br /> The Dragon-Blood to make one social action an unacceptable influence. This charm may only be used once a scene, but is refreshed upon someone failing to overcome his resolve twice.<br /> <br /> CHAOS-WARDING PRANA<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Integrity 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Inviolate Dragon Spirit<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> DEFENSE-FROM-ANATHEMA METHOD<br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Chaos-Warding Prana<br /> Change last sentence of first paragraph to She can also add her Essence to her Resolve if confronted with an Anathema using mind-altering effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:03:15-08:00","id":817884,"title":"","content":"Resistance<br /> <br /> OX-BODY TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: \u2013; Mins: Resistance 2, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Stackable<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> As Solar Charm<br /> <br /> STRENGTH OF STONE TECHNIQUE<br /> Cost: 2m per person; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> MOUNTAIN TOPPLING METHOD<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One action<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Strength of Stone Technique<br /> The Exalt increases his strength by 5 for the purposes of Feats of Strength. He also increases his Strength by 5 or his essence whichever is lower for withering attacks made with Jade weapons.<br /> <br /> IMPERVIOUS SKIN OF STONE MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 1m per 2 soak; Mins: Resistance 3, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Strength of Stone Technique<br /> Remove &quot;Bashing and lethal&quot;<br /> <br /> (ELEMENT) PROTECTION FORM<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Elemental, Stackable<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Impervious Skin of Stone Meditation<br /> This is 5 charms one for each element. Gain soak against attacks of that element equal to the Exalts Essence. Ignore Environmental effect appropriate to the selected element.<br /> Air: Soak increased vs blue jade weapons, and ranged attacks and Ignores cold<br /> Earth: Soak increased vs melee and martial arts attacks made with metal weapons, white jade weapons, Ignores falling damage<br /> Fire: Soak increased vs firewands and red jade, immune to heat but not flame<br /> Water: Soak increased vs black jade and all attacks while under water, allows the exalt to breath underwater<br /> Wood: Soak increased vs melee and martial arts attacks made with wood weapons, green jade weapons, and immune to all natural poisons.<br /> <br /> The soak bonus granted by this Charm does not apply to attacks enhanced by Charms or Sorcery of Celestial level or higher, but it is applicable to elementally aspected Charms such<br /> as Elemental Bolt Attack. Also, the soak benefits do not apply against artifact weapons made from magical materials other than whatever form of jade is associated with the element used in the Charm deployed. Normally, the Essence cost is three motes, but when an Exalt is using the version associated with the element of his own Aspect, the cost is only two motes. Using multiple versions of this charm at once does not increase the soak, merely what the soak applies to. This Charm does stack with Impervious Skin of Stone Meditation and is compatible with armor.<br /> <br /> UNEATING EARTH MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Resistance 4, Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One day<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> UNBREATHING EARTH MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Uneating Earth Meditation<br /> No Change<br /> <br /> UNFEELING EARTH MEDITATION<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Resistance 5, Essence 3;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Unbreathing Earth Meditation<br /> No Change<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:14:26-08:00","id":817889,"title":"","content":"Well right off the bat, I noticed that none of the aspects have Brawl as a favored ability. Unless you meant that instead of Martial Arts for Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:18:57-08:00","id":817894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817844-dragonblood-3e-conversion-peach?p=817889#post817889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well right off the bat, I noticed that none of the aspects have Brawl as a favored ability. Unless you meant that instead of Martial Arts for Water.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stupid 2E not having brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:22:09-08:00","id":817896,"title":"","content":"Technically, no one in 3e has Martial Arts. One GETS Martial Arts favored if they select Brawl favored, but Brawl is the default since you need the merit to unlock Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:01:15-08:00","id":817939,"title":"","content":"The thing I noticed was the Air caste getting +Essence to Defense vs archery/thrown attacks. That is a pretty major boost, particularly at high levels where they will be immune to mortal ranged attacks. I would suggest changing it to a -Essence penalty to those attacks instead. It's still a potentially big buff, just not so unbeatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:14:02-08:00","id":817993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817844-dragonblood-3e-conversion-peach?p=817939#post817939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I noticed was the Air caste getting +Essence to Defense vs archery/thrown attacks. That is a pretty major boost, particularly at high levels where they will be immune to mortal ranged attacks. I would suggest changing it to a -Essence penalty to those attacks instead. It's still a potentially big buff, just not so unbeatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go even further and say subtract (Essence/2) in dice from their attacks. It's a stacking defense buff that isn't affected by charm dice caps or anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:48:19-08:00","id":818014,"title":"","content":"Would you be considering writing your own brawl plus Maybe other charms as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:24:05-08:00","id":818082,"title":"","content":"Outcastes shouldn't be getting 5 favoured abilities. I'm even kind of dubious about DBs getting modular caste abilities as it is. They're kind of supposed to be really limited and specialized into their aspects.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about bringing back the breeding merit to give motes, it was kind of something that people got out of necessity rather than being a cool concept for the character. Maybe make it give a bonus to social rolls with people who treat higher breeding DBs with respect? Maybe it should be subsumed into the reputation merit?<br /> <br /> The anima-flux is actually a rule in the third edition core. It does mostly what you said except it is caped at 1 die and also any hardness completely negates both effects.<br /> <br /> I'd say remove Voice of Mastery entirely, effects like this are hard to come by, even in the Solar charmset, this edition.<br /> <br /> I'd also bring Voices on the Wind down to a bas of Essence X 10 feet, and cap it's magnitude by (Essence/2) so at max essence you can get a thousand foot radius, but otherwise you need to be somewhere remotely closeby.<br /> <br /> With One Mind is beyond my current ability to balance in third edition, but I'd say it's definitely too powerful as-is.<br /> <br /> The range on Elemental Bolt Attack can get too high too fast, especially since I don't know if it can be targeted at medium range without aiming. I'd say range equal to (Essence/2)+1 and put in a reminder that attacks beyond short range require an aim action. So it can go short range at essence 1-2, medium at 3-4 and long at 5, with air aspects boosting that a range band each time.<br /> <br /> Elemental burst should never hit more than one range band, hitting everyone in close range of one-another is great enough. Also half the damage on elemental burst.<br /> <br /> I'd add a -2 to attacks made against spirits that you're using Spirit Detecting Mirror to see. Which is a pretty generous interpretation of trying to fight someone you can only see in the reflection of your swordblade<br /> <br /> I'd make the archery disrupting effect of Wind Luring Song as-per my suggestion for air aspect anima, and stipulate that the two effects don't stack<br /> <br /> Ditch Fivefold Resonance Sense's ability to lock on to artifacts attuned to other users. Yeah they're said to be concealed by any magic concealing them, but it lets you perfectly detect somebody who's not using magic to hide themselves<br /> <br /> Change Trackless Passage to a simple penalty, maybe equal to (Stealth/2) dice, the effect as is completely cancels with all Solar tracking charms, among also making it impossible for mortal tracking to happen.<br /> <br /> Dragon Shroud needs to have two effects, one that blurs you, and one that lets you spend motes to get automatic successes on stealth rolls, otherwise it's Infinite Mastery again<br /> <br /> Whirlwind Shield Form should be as it was in the original, that being adding an (essence/2) dice penalty. This should explicitly not stack with air anima similar effects.<br /> <br /> Vengeful Gust Counterattack shouldn't be adding non-charm dice, in fact I'm not sure anything in the DB charmset should be adding non-charm dice/successes, and also I kind of thought the counterattack effect was cool, maybe leave it more as it was in 2e? Where if the person successfully parries an attack, then you counter attack with a number of dice equal to the number of successes that they failed to hit you by?<br /> <br /> Deadly Blades of the Five Dragons, air aspects absolutely need an aim action, maybe make it extend an extra range band?<br /> <br /> Elemental Armor, Fire Aspects shouldn't increase their anima damage, I think nothing in the DB charmset should actually do that. Maybe just boost the damage of your weapon by 1-2? Also the Water one is way too good, at best it should reduce onslaught penalties by one. The wood one I'd say leave it at withering attacks gain 1 less initiative, the reset to base number of 3 is really important and shouldn't be messed with<br /> <br /> Sense-Riding Technique should have a time limit of Essence hours or something, and should probably have a more hefty penalty to normal actions on their end of it.<br /> <br /> Sense-Destroying Method should have a cap, maybe (awareness)? And not be able to take a person's sense completely unless it somehow gives a penalty equal to their whole dicepool<br /> <br /> Essence Disruption Attack is just straight up too good in any form for third edition<br /> <br /> Flaw-Finding Examination probably shouldn't be reducing a major repair to one minute. Half the time maybe?<br /> <br /> Flaw-Finding Exploitation shouldn't affect artifacts.<br /> <br /> Charms of Unmaking really shouldn't be giving craft experience. That turns them into a massive sxp engine. At best maybe gain 1sxp from unmaking things, if making it would have triggered an objective? As is they're already really powerful effects that can effect artifacts with high enough essence.<br /> <br /> Unflagging Vengeance Motivation, Unnatural Influence isn't really a thing anymore, maybe he just ignores charms with the Psyche keyword? It also probably shouldn't counter magical fatigue, and definitely shouldn't be adding integrity to his soak.<br /> <br /> Granite Curtain of Serenity should probably only be instant or action long, even Solars don't really get scenelong buffs like that anymore<br /> <br /> Inviolate Dragon Spirit should add some bonus to his resolve, maybe equal to the intimacy's resolve bonus that he brought to bear? If it's 10m 1wp it might even be a candidate for non-charm successes.<br /> <br /> Defense from Anathema Method maybe should be removed, but if it stays in then it's defense bonuses need to be at least halved<br /> <br /> Ox-Body Technique should take off a -2 health level at stage of it's Stamina progression. Stamina 1-2=(-1) || Stamina 3-4=(-1,-2) || Stamina 5=(-0,-2)<br /> <br /> Mountain Toppling Method definitely needs to have it's withering damage value pulled back to two or three bonus damage on withering attacks with jade weapons<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OKAY! Well that took a while, other than all that though I'd say it's good! I like what you did with (Element) Protection Form! Anyway, It must have taken a super long time to write all these out, good work and keep at it! Don't take my criticisms too harshly either, there's just a lot of new stuff in this edition, like the aim action and scenelong dice buffs, that don't seem that important, but are actually super mega important and shouldn't be screwed around with lightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}